==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|Shanks' pony}}
* {{l|en|shanks's pony}}, {{l|en|shank's pony}}, {{l|en|shanks pony}}

===Etymology===
Believed to be of Scottish origin, from {{m|en|shanks' nag}} ({{m|en|shanks-naig}}, attested 1774).

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[shank]]s' [[pony]]|-}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic|UK|Australia|New Zealand}} One's feet or legs, regarded as a means of transport.
#*'''1930''', G. E. O. Knight, ''Intimate Glimpses of Mysterious Tibet and Neighbouring Countries'', 1992, [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=hDQ1Kds0NScC&pg=PA56&lpg=PA56&dq=%22shanks%27+pony%22+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&source=bl&ots=zksYR27A14&sig=sasa0_i2E7g4ywlYJ1OcF9Pp8WI&hl=en&sa=X&ei=tjFCUOfQC8iRiQfpooHABg&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22shanks%27%20pony%22%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false page 56],
#*: {{...}}pointed out that we cared nothing, absolutely nothing, for convention, and would go in quest of the gods “on '''Shanks′ pony''',” Anqui utterly mistook our meaning and had a pony in waiting for us when the hour came for leaving! This we dismissed after attempting to make clear our meaning.
#* '''1989''', [[w:Charles Hyatt|Charles Hyatt]], ''When Me Was a Boy'', Institute of Jamaica Publications, [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=q6cjIgrIVJwC&pg=PA43&lpg=PA43&dq=%22shanks%27+pony%22+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&source=bl&ots=GwcGNBx_Tp&sig=TI67RmfTIGoEAUN0cQRm06ZclFA&hl=en&sa=X&ei=tjFCUOfQC8iRiQfpooHABg&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22shanks%27%20pony%22%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false page 43],
#*: After all, mos′ everybody had to walk because yuh doan only get to meet people but ‘'''shanks pony'''’ was the cheapes′ form of transportation.
#* '''1993''', [[w:John Marsden (writer)|John Marsden]], ''[[w:Tomorrow, When the War Began|Tomorrow, When the War Began]]'', [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=h6RSRK71PTMC&pg=PT22&lpg=PT22&dq=%22shanks%27+pony%22+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&source=bl&ots=qpHkc8yigD&sig=yPiKl_3c-Ej-Aw5k6d3SQkiMnPA&hl=en&sa=X&ei=tjFCUOfQC8iRiQfpooHABg&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22shanks%27%20pony%22%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false page 18],
#*: That was the end of the vehicle track: from then on it was '''shanks′s pony'''.
